course: dictionary
lesson: 14008
title: Lunchroom: where we eat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lunchroom is a room where people eat lunch. In a school or a workplace, it is the room with tables and chairs where everyone sits down to eat together.
explain: «The class lined up outside the lunchroom at twelve o'clock.» The words lined up and at twelve o'clock are clues. People queue to get food at lunchtime, so a lunchroom must be the room for eating lunch.
explain: Lunchroom is mainly used in American and Canadian English. In Britain, children often say dinner hall, canteen or dining hall. In Australia, many children eat their lunch outside. Different words, same idea: a place to eat lunch.
fact: A lunchroom is a room in a school or workplace where people eat lunch.
fact: «Please wash your hands before you go into the lunchroom.» Washing hands is one of the lunchroom rules.
fact: Other lunchroom rules: line up, and clean up your tray when you have finished.
fact: Lunchroom is mainly American and Canadian English. British schools more often say dinner hall, canteen or dining hall.
fact: Useful phrases: «lunchroom monitor» and «eat in the lunchroom».
exercise: «Mia put her tray back at the end of the lunchroom.» What is a lunchroom? | An outdoor playground | *A room where people eat lunch | A room where people sleep | A room for music lessons
exercise: Which of these is a rule for the lunchroom? | Throw your food at your friends | *Wash your hands before you eat | Run between the tables and shout | Leave your tray on the floor
exercise: Sam is from Britain. What might he call the same room? | Gymnasium | Bus stop | Library | *Dinner hall
test: «Our class eats in the lunchroom every day at half past twelve.» Where do the children eat? | In the library | *In the lunchroom | Under the stage | On the bus
test: Lunchroom is mainly used in which places? | Only in maths lessons | Only in ancient Roman texts | *American and Canadian English | Only in Scottish towns
exam: Which sentence uses lunchroom correctly? | Please lunchroom the book on the shelf. | The lunchroom is a type of cloud that brings rain. | *The whole class ate their lunch in the lunchroom. | The lunchroom was very loud and quiet at once.
